  "question_count": 5,
  "summary": "Why this pipeline\n\u2022 Invoice payment confirmation. Match bank statement receipts to the customer invoice register by customer name, check whether the amount paid matches the invoice total, and tell me for each invoice if it is paid, short, overpaid, or not paid.\n\nWhat each step does\n1. Bank_Statement_June \u2014 Reads working file Bank_Statement_June.xlsx and detects its columns.\n2. Customer_Invoices \u2014 Reads working file Customer_Invoices.xlsx and detects its columns.\n3. AR_Collections_Policy \u2014 Reads the policy/reference file AR_Collections_Policy.pdf and keeps the rules for matching and review.\n4. Matcher \u2014 Pairs rows that share payer_name, customer_name. Dates may drift by 15 day(s). Leftovers and splits go to exceptions.\n5. Math \u2014 Applies: abs(actual - expected) > min(0.01 * expected, 50.00).\n6. Decision \u2014 Flags or approves using: Flag duplicate payments, cite the AR collections policy, and escalate invoices unpaid more than 30 days past due..\n7. Output \u2014 Builds a Excel report you can download.",
  "extra": {
    "onboarding_step": "done",
    "role": "AR collections analyst on the O2C team",
    "industry": "Manufacturing \u2014 mid-market industrial, USD only",
    "ai_priorities": "Confirm which customer invoices actually got paid from the bank feed, and surface shorts and unpaid items.",
    "description": "Invoice payment confirmation. Match bank statement receipts to the customer invoice register by customer name, check whether the amount paid matches the invoice total, and tell me for each invoice if it is paid, short, overpaid, or not paid.",
    "knowledge_facts": [
      {
        "id": "fact_1",
        "kind": "entity",
        "value": "Helios Industrial",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-e8ba05333a"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_2",
        "kind": "constraint",
        "value": "The invoice register is the source of truth for what is owed, and bank statements contain unrelated operating items that must not be treated as customer receipts.",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-9e0bb249f8"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_3",
        "kind": "constraint",
        "value": "Pair invoice rows to bank receipts on customer name / payer name using semantic normalization; do not use amount as a match key.",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-59ca61c8d7"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_4",
        "kind": "threshold",
        "value": "Allow the lesser of 1% of the invoice total or USD 50.00 as an amount tolerance.",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-f8f929a7a4"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_5",
        "kind": "formula",
        "value": "abs(actual \u2212 expected) > min(0.01 \u00d7 expected, 50.00)",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-f8f929a7a4"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_6",
        "kind": "constraint",
        "value": "A second payment of the same invoice amount is a duplicate and must be flagged.",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-fb632b3129"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_7",
        "kind": "threshold",
        "value": "Invoices with no bank receipt that are past due more than 30 calendar days escalate for collections.",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-abe0b2a87a"
      },
      {
        "id": "fact_8",
        "kind": "expected_outcome",
        "value": "Excel workbook with a sheet per outcome: matched (paid), residuals (partial / split leftovers), exceptions (unpaid, duplicate, out-of-tolerance).",
        "chunk_id": "AR_Collections_Policy-365ada6571"
      }
    ],
    "node_overrides": {
      "math": {
        "catalog_id": "min_pct_amount_tolerance",
        "input_map": {
          "actual": "amount",
          "expected": "total_amount"
        },
        "constants": {
          "pct": 0.01,
          "amount": 50
        },
        "formula_en": "abs(actual - expected) > min(0.01 * expected, 50.00)",
        "shape": "sequential",
        "mode": "hybrid",
        "ast": "abs(actual - expected)",
        "gate_ast": "abs(actual - expected) > min(pct * expected, amount)",
        "output_column": "over_tolerance",
        "compiled_from": "abs(actual - expected) > min(0.01 * expected, 50.00)"
