    "pipeline_brief": "Why this pipeline\n\u2022 Invoice payment confirmation. Match bank statement receipts to the customer invoice register by customer name, check whether the amount paid matches the invoice total, and tell me for each invoice if it is paid, short, overpaid, or not paid.\n\nWhat each step does\n1. Bank_Statement_June \u2014 Reads working file Bank_Statement_June.xlsx and detects its columns.\n2. Customer_Invoices \u2014 Reads working file Customer_Invoices.xlsx and detects its columns.\n3. AR_Collections_Policy \u2014 Reads the policy/reference file AR_Collections_Policy.pdf and keeps the rules for matching and review.\n4. Matcher \u2014 Pairs rows that share payer_name, customer_name. Dates may drift by 15 day(s). Leftovers and splits go to exceptions.\n5. Math \u2014 Applies: abs(actual - expected) > min(0.01 * expected, 50.00).\n6. Decision \u2014 Flags or approves using: Flag duplicate payments, cite the AR collections policy, and escalate invoices unpaid more than 30 days past due..\n7. Output \u2014 Builds a Excel report you can download."
